From 38fbb1c31d929c0afd316e8035991d9833fecd80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bugcheck <bugcheck@local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:02:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fences: side-yard and shared rear fences between neighbouring
 houses

Yasin 7 Nov: fences between homes don't follow a good logic, most of them are missing. Fences
existed only along the 141 alleys (back lot lines) plus 26 OSM barrier ways; no side-yard fences.
fences_alleys.json gets 'side' (bugcheck1/tools/side_fences.py, from npc/data/homes.json doors +
street normals, home footprint rects / fence_bldg_mask.json, alleys):
- neighbours on the same street side (normals within ~30 deg, front lines within 10 m), next along
  the street; fence down the middle of the footprint gap (1.2-20 m), from 2 m behind the more
  recessed front facade to 7 m behind the deeper house (max 38 m), 1.5 m short of an alley
- rear fence joining the two side fences' back corners where no alley runs within 8 m
- stucco wall when both houses are Spanish / stucco style, else picket
1474 side + 541 rear fences (26.1 + 7.9 km). The loader reads 'side' like the OSM ways (3 m pieces,
dropped on asphalt / driveways / inside buildings, colliders, per-cell merged mesh).
Measured (override pack, packs mounted): fence length 18.5 -> 48.4 km, island fence tris 197k ->
413k (per 200 m cell, one draw each as before), setup 193 -> 346 ms at load. Rendered: side fences
between houses at I Ave / residential east.
